   181	What SKILL.state removes is the need to **reconstruct** the state from history. What it
   182	introduces is the need to **write** it correctly at every transition, and nothing in the
   183	runtime checks that the write matches what the action did. Gemini's belief never departed
   184	from reality in any of its 75 episodes; Haiku wrote at least one wrong patch in 17 of 24
   185	at T=200, and in 7 of them the error reached a decision. The paper's thesis survives in
   186	direction — SKILL.state is still the best arm on Gemini and within 0.02 of ReAct on
   187	Haiku — but "explicit state does not degrade" is a property of the model as much as of
   188	the runtime.
