   361	## 5. Two probes on their declared limitations
   362	
   363	The paper declares two limitations without measuring them. We measured them.
   364	
   365	### L1: explicit state only protects what was anticipated
   366	
   367	A fact arrives at step `t` and changes the correct action at `t+40`; the measure is
   368	whether the agent gets that one step right. All three models, T=50, seeds 0–2 × 8
   369	repetitions per cell, output cap 8192 (Gemini with reasoning budget 0), Claude via
   370	Microsoft Foundry and Gemini via Vertex, with a runner that applies no action when the
   371	runtime returns none (§6, item 11). SKILL.state under four schema conditions:
   372	
   373	| Condition | Haiku 4.5 | Sonnet 5 | Gemini 3 Flash |
   374	|---|---|---|---|
   375	| No field to store it | 0/24 [0–14 %] | 3/24 [4–31 %] | 0/24 [0–14 %] |
   376	| Free-form `notes` field | 10/24 [24–61 %] | 8/24 [18–53 %] | 0/24 [0–14 %] |
   377	| Schema field naming the fact | **24/24 [86–100 %]** | **18/24 [55–88 %]** | **16/24 [47–82 %]** |
   378	| Reminder attached to the observation | **24/24 [86–100 %]** | **20/24 [64–93 %]** | 8/24 [18–53 %] |
   379	
   380	ReAct has no schema, so the first three conditions send it the identical prompt; pooled,
   381	they are 72 replicates of the same cell. Its reminder condition is the only one that
   382	changes what it sees:
   383	
   384	| ReAct | Haiku 4.5 | Sonnet 5 | Gemini 3 Flash |
   385	|---|---|---|---|
   386	| No reminder (72 runs) | 10/72 = 14 % [8–24 %] | 20/72 = 28 % [19–39 %] | 0/72 = 0 % [0–5 %] |
   387	| Reminder on the observation | **18/24 = 75 % [55–88 %]** | **23/24 = 96 % [80–99 %]** | **17/24 = 71 % [51–85 %]** |
