   420	### L2: retroactive invalidation
   421	
   422	An announced fact stops being true later, and the agent has to act on the correction.
   423	On a correct trajectory the correction decides **exactly one step per episode**; once an
   424	agent misses it, its world diverges and further steps start to disagree with the truth,
   425	so counting them scores the cascade, not the correction. The measure is therefore per
   426	episode: does the agent get the decisive step right? All three models at T=50, seeds 4,
   427	10 and 6 × 8 repetitions, output cap 8192 (Gemini with reasoning budget 0), Claude via
   428	Microsoft Foundry and Gemini via Vertex:
   429	
   430	| Model | ReAct applies the correction | SKILL.state |
   431	|---|---|---|
   432	| Haiku 4.5 | 1/24 | **24/24** |
   433	| Sonnet 5 | 9/24 | **22/24** |
   434	| Gemini 3 Flash | 0/24 | **24/24** |
