   437	90–99 %); full history in 10 of 72 (14 %, 8–24 %).** Every episode had its decisive step,
   438	and no response was truncated at it — seven Sonnet/ReAct episodes truncated elsewhere,
   439	and none was excluded. The misses are not other errors: every failed decisive step is
   440	exactly the action of an agent that never heard the correction. The successes
   441	concentrate by scenario rather than by trial — Sonnet with ReAct scores 2/8, 0/8 and
   442	7/8 across the three seeds, and its two SKILL.state misses are both in seed 4 — so the
   443	binomial intervals understate the uncertainty of generalising to new scenarios.
   444	
