   454	
   455	Gemini with ReAct never applies either correction — 0 of 72 in L1 without a reminder, 0
   456	of 24 in L2 — while scoring 0.913 on the long procedure; Haiku scores 0.974 at T=200 and
   457	applies the L2 correction once in 24. What holds on all three models is that **the
   458	long-procedure score does not predict this failure, and within each model the runtime
   459	decides it.** Both probes are measured with the same cap and design on the three models;
   460	their decoding still differs between providers (§3).
