   464	## 6. Instrument and artefacts
   465	
   466	This is the section that separates this from a blog post, and the one that cost us most.
   467	
   468	**Nine artefacts catalogued** in the first block, all with the same signature: an
   469	implicit contract between runtime and model. The runtime assumed something it never
   470	declared, and the result depended on whether the model guessed right. The first three
   471	cost entire grids; **two surfaced in the audit before publication, and both had produced
   472	a written result, with tables and intervals, ready to send**.
   473	
   474	This second block added six more, and they are worth enumerating because they transfer:
   475	
   476	1. **Greedy decoding does not guarantee reproducibility.** The protocol assumed that at
   477	   `temperature=0` seeds are environment instances and one run per cell suffices. The
   478	   same cell repeated five times gives between 0.830 and 0.960. **Three already-written
   479	   conclusions collapsed on repetition**: an environment effect of −5.8 points that
   480	   turned out to be +0.008, a "monotonic" noise curve that turned out flat, and a
   481	   noise estimate of eleven points that turned out to be a tail.
   482	2. **The distribution has a left tail because failures cascade.** Across five runs of one
   483	   cell the sample deviation is 0.052; **excluding the 0.830 outlier** it is 0.012, and
   484	   three runs of the same cell at T=100 give 0.006. We quote both, because the second
   485	   number is conditional on removing the very run that motivates the point. What forces
   486	   repetition is not the ordinary spread: it is the tails.
   487	3. **The runner discarded the model's responses.** It kept the score and the token
   488	   counts, so `correct=False` was an indistinguishable zero: you could not tell whether
   489	   the model lost track of state — what the experiment measures — or miscopied a JSON
   490	   field. With responses retained, adjudicating 45 failures across four traces of one
   491	   cell gives **32 wrong-shelf (71 %), 7 wrong action type (16 %), 5 field-copy errors
   492	   (11 %), 1 unparseable**.
   493	4. **A truncated episode counted as complete.** Aggregation counted files, not steps; an
   494	   episode of 163 steps out of 200 entered the mean. The bias was two thousandths, but
   495	   it was only found because completeness was checked as a matter of routine.
   496	5. **Traces that did not record their own conditions.** For most of this work the traces
   497	   stored no output cap, reasoning budget, provider or responding model ID. Two files
   498	   from the same cell could come from different caps and nothing would say so — which is
   499	   how a −5.8-point "environment effect" survived long enough to be written down. The
   500	   runners now write a conditions header and per-step token usage — but **only runs made
   501	   after that change carry it**. The historical Gemini traces — Table 1 except the
   502	   Stateful re-measurement, the noise table and the environment comparison — do not, so
   503	   their conditions are certified by the filename and the run log, not by the artefact
   504	   itself. Every trace behind the Haiku table, both Stateful re-measurements, the Memory
   505	   control and the prompt-order experiment does.
   506	6. **A probe that measured the wrong pattern.** The cache probe repeated an identical
   507	   request and concluded that Vertex has no implicit cache, while the project's own
   508	   grids recorded 503,600 cached tokens in one episode. The probe was correct; the
   509	   pattern it probed was not the one the experiment uses.
   510	
   511	A third block, found while measuring the second model, contains the most expensive
   512	artefact of the project:
   513	
   514	7. **One of the four arms never ran.** Stateful read its state patch with a non-greedy
   515	   regex that stopped at the first closing brace. Every nested patch — the normal case,
   516	   `{"shelf_contents": {"3": {...}}}` — was truncated, failed to parse, and was dropped
   517	   without a warning: **40 of 5,775 responses on Gemini produced an applied patch, 0 of
   518	   6,000 on Haiku**. What both
   519	   Stateful columns measured is full history plus a state block with no inventory — empty
   520	   on Haiku, and on Gemini holding only the occasional `last_event` (the 40 patches, in
   521	   11 episodes). Its unit test
   522	   used a flat value and passed. It surfaced only because Stateful beat SKILL.state on
   523	   Haiku and we went to the traces to find out why. Re-measured with the parser fixed,
   524	   no change was detected (§3). The first fix was itself incomplete: on Haiku it still
   525	   dropped every patch written in Markdown — 731 of 3,000 at T=200 — which the third
   526	   adversarial review found, not us; a third parser version closed it. A defect that
   527	   changes nothing measurable is still a defect in what the column claims to measure.
   528	8. **A cap one model respects and the other does not.** The summariser's own cap was
   529	   never reached on Gemini and was exceeded in half the summaries on Haiku (§3). A cap
   530	   is not a neutral constant across models; it has to be checked per model, in the
   531	   traces.
   532	9. **Resuming re-paid finished work.** The completeness check counted the conditions
   533	   header as a step, so no episode ever matched its horizon and every relaunch re-ran
   534	   episodes already measured. It was caught on the first relaunch of R2 because a cell
   535	   finished minutes earlier started again.
   536	10. **The traces did not record cache writes.** The client received them; the trace row
   537	    did not store them. In the first run of the prompt-order experiment the arm that
   538	    rewrites its cache every step — the most expensive case — showed ~540 prompt tokens
   539	    per step and looked the cheapest. Those twelve episodes were discarded and re-run.
   540	    The §4 table does not depend on it: it was computed by the grid runner, which counted
   541	    writes.
   542	
   543	11. **A probe that could not fail.** The first L2 scorer counted dependent steps on a
   544	    simulated trajectory and subtracted only deaf actions, and its runner repaired the
   545	    world whenever the runtime returned no action; a runtime that never answers scored
   546	    100 %. It was the section of this draft we had checked least, because its result was
   547	    the cleanest. The fifth adversarial review found it. Re-measured with the decisive
   548	    step read from the real trajectory, explicit state goes from "132 of 132" to 70 of
   549	    72 episodes. L1 had the same world-repairing runner; re-measured, its cells barely
   550	    moved, but only the new traces could show that.
   551	
   552	Items 5 and 6 were found by an **independent adversarial review of this draft against
   553	the raw traces**, not by us. That review also corrected the failure classification
   554	above, the maintenance-event range in §2, the compression factor in §3 and the sample
   555	size in §3. We recommend the procedure, not the anecdote: have something recompute every
   556	published figure from the artefacts, without access to the prose that justifies it.
   557	
   558	Why traces matter, verbatim from one episode: at step 12 the model stores the SKU of a
   559	different pallet; at step 16 it asserts *"Shelf 0 (SKU-F, stored in step 12)"* when it
   560	had itself stored SKU-B there. **The early error contaminates later decisions** — and
   561	that, not sampling noise, is what produces the tail.
   562	
   563	**The transferable claim**: the paper treats the runtime as neutral infrastructure — a
   564	merge operator, a patch format, a schema, a prompt order. In this project, individual
   565	runtime decisions moved results by amounts comparable to or larger than the difference
   566	between the methods being compared: the schema field decides 0 % versus 67 % on the
   567	dependent step (§5), and a parser that silently dropped state patches decided what one
   568	of four arms measured until it was fixed (§6, item 7). We have not measured every such
   569	decision, so we make no claim about a general range.
   570	
   571	**Repository artefacts**: environment with fidelity flags, per-step traces, completeness
   572	verifier, a density meter that does not call the API, truncation counters, per-episode
   573	checkpointing and end-to-end cache accounting.
   574	
   575	---
   576	
   577	## 7. Limitations
   578	
   579	- **`gemini-3-flash-preview` may not be their `Gemini-3-Flash`.** Declared as a risk
   580	  from the outset. Vertex returns the responding model ID on every call and it is
   581	  recorded per step, but not in the traces measured before that change. The Anthropic
   582	  client did not copy it until the last Stateful re-measurement: from then on — its 30
   583	  episodes and the prompt-order experiment — every step records
   584	  `claude-haiku-4-5-20251001`; the earlier Haiku traces record only the requested alias
   585	  in their header.
   586	- **A reimplemented environment is not their environment.** We matched what their
   587	  appendix allows us to compare, and the remaining differences are in §2. The shelf
   588	  choice in `Store` still awaits an answer from the authors.
   589	- **Our Memory is not comparable to theirs.** Our summariser compresses fourteen times
   590	  more (5,770-token mean prompt against their 84,364 at T=200).
   591	  What we measured is our summarisation policy, not "summarisation" as a category.
   592	- **We have not proven the environment gaps have no effect.** The measured difference is
   593	  +0.009, with an interval of roughly −0.040 to +0.057 (§2): no change was detected, and
   594	  effects of several points in either direction remain compatible. The same caveat
   595	  applies to the three lowest noise levels in §3.
   596	- **Cell sizes are not uniform.** Nineteen cells carry 15 runs; ReAct at T=200 carries
   597	  19, unbalanced across seeds (3/3/7/3/3). Five of its episodes exist only as
   598	  aggregates, without traces.
   599	- **Cost figures price input only**, and the caching results depend on the length of the
   600	  static prefix (§4).
   601	- **The probes share cap and design across models, not decoding.** Both were re-measured
   602	  on all three models with the corrected runner (§5); Gemini runs with temperature 0 and
   603	  reasoning budget 0, Claude without either setting.
   604	- **One environment.** The second (Software Repository) was retired because it could not
   605	  measure what it was built for, not because the arms scored alike — they did not
   606	  (Haiku: SKILL.state 0.974, ReAct 0.895; Sonnet: 0.876 and 1.000, 9 episodes each). Its
   607	  dependency always sat exactly two steps after the event that created it, so it had no
   608	  delayed relevance to measure; all four arms applied that rule (Haiku SKILL.state 14/15,
   609	  ReAct 12/12; Sonnet SKILL.state 12/13, ReAct all); and the score differences came from
   610	  routine steps, not from the rule (`docs/resultados-bloque1.md`, §4.ter).
   611	- **SKILL.state's ceiling depends on the model.** At 1.000 with zero variance on Gemini
   612	  the task did not discriminate at the top; on Haiku it does (0.958 at T=200), and the
   613	  failure is in writing the state (§3). Two models are not enough to say which models
   614	  make that error.
   615	- **Stateful has been re-measured only at T=50 and T=200**, with parser version 2 on
   616	  Gemini (which applied 3,748 of 3,750 of its patches) and version 3 on Haiku. The
   617	  intermediate horizons of Gemini's Table 1 keep the defective measurement, marked as
   618	  such.
   619	- **Haiku and Gemini do not share decoding settings** (§3): the cross-model differences
   620	  are between two configured systems, not two models under identical conditions.
   621	- **Haiku's Memory column mixes the summarisation policy with summary truncation** (§3);
   622	  the control arm has n=9 and bounds the effect at T=50 only.

